# Always commit and push

Owner instruction (2026-08-16): do not wait for a separate "commit and push"
ask. When a slice is locally done (`bash scripts/verify.sh` green, ledgers
updated), commit and push in the same turn.

Then follow CLAUDE.md rule 5: start `bash scripts/ci-status.sh` after the
push, prove the Vercel deploy reached READY, and fetch a live marker. A
green local verify is not shipped.

Owner standing order (2026-09-03, DECISIONS #636): land completed slices
on `main` the same turn. The owner checks www.aimplifi.app, not a pull
request. An unmerged PR is unshipped. Merge the PR in the same turn; do
not wait to be asked again. Do not merge a PR that is conflicting or
whose verify is red. Cloud agents do not write to `C:\dev\Aimplifi`.

Do not force-push `main`. Do not skip hooks. Do not commit secrets, `.next`,
or `test-results`.
